\",\n    \"Put a priority order and a stopping point in the prompt, for example a must-have list and a list of what may be cut, and say which features the goal's 'done' condition requires.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"American Football Fiasco\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Call it, snap it, hit it, win the Cup\",\n    \"description\": \"The Tumbleweed Junction Fiascos have lost 99 games in a row, and the owner has bet the field on the Fiasco Cup. Call plays from big cards, then run, pass and hit your way down a seven-a-side field.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"American football (over the top arcade style)\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick moves; J throws or hands off; K juke or dive; L hits; hold Shift for turbo; Q switches defenders\",\n    \"tags\": [\"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"story\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1,"newLines":51,"lines":[" {","-  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"\"},","-  \"testingFeedback\": [],","-  \"engineFeedback\": [],","-  \"promptFeedback\": [],","-  \"aiHub\": {\"name\": \"\", \"tagline\": \"\", \"description\": \"\", \"type\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"series\": \"\", \"players\": \"\", \"controls\": \"\", \"tags\": []}","+  \"sourceInformation\": {","+    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 07:16:27\",","+    \"source\": \"American football (over the top arcade style)\",","+    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",","+    \"genre\": \"Arcade sports (American football), with beat-'em-up hit feel and a light story campaign (THE FIASCO CUP)\",","+    \"perspective\": \"Three-quarter camera from the sideline, following the ball, zoomable\",","+    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (handoff package, commit 4390a9852fe0, with three small changes logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md), vanilla JavaScript, Canvas 2D and Web Audio; Playwright 1.63.0 for the browser checks; no CDN or libraries\",","+    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's native look: HD Humanoid rigs drawn as pixel art at res ps1 (320x240, expanded to the window), procedural turf with yard lines, stands with a crowd, lights, sprites and particles\",","+    \"animation\": \"The engine's Humanoid rig with its own poses (run, down, cheer, wince), driven from the match each step; no motion-capture clips\",","+    \"audio\": \"All music, sound effects and voices written in code: a bouncing field song, a title theme, synthesized sound effects, and Animalese babble voices for the radio\",","+    \"online\": \"none (planned through the AI Hub Session Protocol; not built in this session)\",","+    \"testing\": \"Headless tests in a Node VM (test/run.mjs: boot, sim, whole match, attract, dev, cup) and Playwright screenshots (tools/shots.mjs)\",","+    \"research\": \"none (the engine's API card and its sports kit were read; no web research)\",","+    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium 1243 through Playwright\",","+    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",","+    \"usage\": \"unknown\"","+  },","+  \"testingFeedback\": [","+    \"Testing caught four issues: the ball was never marked as held, so no tackle or touchdown could end a play and the whole match stalled in live play; the radio's dialog was never ticked, so its lines never typed; a scene change needed a no-fade option for the tests to see it; and the Dev mode's dialog ran its update before its scene was entered. Screenshots caught four more: the camera was too close to read the field, the controller prompts ran across the field, the hot-streak line used a glyph the pixel font lacks, and the radio box covered the call's hint. Reading the engine caught the PlayStation symbols missing from the font and a roster order that did not match the formations.\",","+    \"Two were critical: the match stalled (no play ever ended, so no score was possible), and the radio was silent. The stall was fixed and the whole match now runs to the final whistle in every headless run. Nothing else found was game breaking.\",","+    \"The most helpful test was the whole-match run: the CPU calls for both sides through four quarters and the test checks that the match ends, scores, and passes through every phase. It found the stall at once.\",","+    \"The least helpful was the boot suite: it passed on the first try and checks only that the files load and the title is the first scene.\"","+  ],","+  \"engineFeedback\": [","+    \"The Humanoid rig with its poses and the E.Menu, E.Dialog and Game APIs did most of the work, and game.advance with game.debug made the match testable in a plain Node VM.\",","+    \"Yes. Scene changes fade by default, so a test that did not wait saw the old scene. E.Dialog needs its update called every step, which the API card implies but does not say. The PlayStation symbols were not in the pixel font, and the glyph setting defaulted to Auto rather than PlayStation. The E.Menu y option is a number, which the card does not make clear.\",","+    \"The match itself: the downs and distance, the play calls, the QB and the throws, the catches and picks, the carriers, the tackles and Big Hits, the fumbles, the phases, and the CPU's roles, all in the simulation file.\",","+    \"The 67 KB card and the 1.2 MB engine file took the most time: finding the right names for the rig, the menus, the dialog and the settings meant reading the source in several places.\",","+    \"Three changes, logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md: E1 adds the PlayStation symbols to the 5x7 pixel font, E2 makes PlayStation the default glyph set, and E5 lets a Dialog voice be a function so each letter can have its own pitch.\",","+    \"A Dialog that updates itself from the game's loop, so a scene does not have to tick it, and a way to show a pad's symbols in the font for every label without a patch.\"","+  ],","+  \"promptFeedback\": [","+    \"The shape of the exit interview and the list of what each section needs; the list of TASK.md features gives a clear checklist.\",","+    \"How much the plan asks for in one session: it is over 2,500 lines and names several full systems (online play, a broadcast camera, a story, couch co-op) with no cut order. The folder naming also mixes the plan's model name with the STAGE's.\",","+    \"Fitting the whole plan into one session. I built the core match, the cup, the attract mode, the Dev mode, and the About screen, and cut the online play, the couch co-op, the laterals, the mascots, the replays and most of the plan's other systems.\",","+    \"Put a priority order and a stopping point in the prompt, for example a must-have list and a list of what may be cut, and say which features the goal's 'done' condition requires.\"","+  ],","+  \"aiHub\": {","+    \"name\": \"American Football Fiasco\",","+    \"tagline\": \"Call it, snap it, hit it, win the Cup\",","+    \"description\": \"The Tumbleweed Junction Fiascos have lost 99 games in a row, and the owner has bet the field on the Fiasco Cup. Call plays from big cards, then run, pass and hit your way down a seven-a-side field.\",","+    \"type\": \"Game\",","+    \"genre\": \"Sports\",","+    \"source\": \"American football (over the top arcade style)\",","+    \"series\": \"\",","+    \"players\": \"1\",","+    \"controls\": \"Stick moves; J throws or hands off; K juke or dive; L hits; hold Shift for turbo; Q switches defenders\",","+    \"tags\": [\"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"story\"]","+  }"," }"]}],"originalFile":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [],\n  \"aiHub\": {\"name\": \"\", \"tagline\": \"\", \"description\": \"\", \"type\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"series\": \"\", \"players\": \"\", \"controls\": \"\", \"tags\": []}\n}\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015f9QAq5id9UcwsdUwPD7UN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
