{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4RfpPbGd3Jf8uHmy2z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is playable, but the goal is not met. The brief asks for every feature in TASK.md, and I built a reduced vertical slice. I'm stopping here rather than claiming completion.\n\n**What's in place**\n- `AmericanFootballFiasco-AmericanFootball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-071627.html` in the work folder. It is a single self-contained file (1.3 MB, no network) and runs from `file://` with no page errors.\n- `exit-interview.json` beside it, parsed and checked for every field.\n- The dev folder `AmericanFootballFiasco-AmericanFootball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-071627/` holds the source, `test/run.mjs` (the one test command: 27 checks, all passing), `tools/shots.mjs`, and `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n- Built: a seven-a-side match with play cards, downs and distance, a clock, passes and catches, tackles, Big Hits, mega hits, fumbles, and scoring. Also: THE FIASCO CUP (five chapters with radio text), Exhibition, Practice (a match with no clock, not real drills), the title, the attract mode (the AI plays and any input exits), the Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and a reset, Hall of Fiasco, About and Credits, a touch-only notice, PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option, and Animalese radio voices.\n\n**What's not built**\n- Online play through AI Hub, and couch co-op for 2–4 players.\n- Laterals, mascots, referees, late hits, LIGHTS OUT, the Fiasco Meter and Cards, the replay and highlight reel, the broadcast camera director, the Play Lab, and the flying helmet.\n- Mouse aiming on the field.\n- Balance is unverified. In a scripted run where the human never acts, the CPU wins 48–7 and fumbles about 13 times a match.\n- Touch-only detection is untested on a real touch device.\n\n**Engine changes** (logged in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`): E1 adds the PlayStation symbols to the pixel font; E2 makes PlayStation the default glyph set; E5 lets a dialog voice be a function.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- Seven a side, with the simplified rules in the plan.\n- The folder and deliverable names use the STAGE's model name, not the plan's.\n- \"Series\" is left empty in the AI Hub entry, as the STAGE allows.\n\n---\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 07:16:27\n- Source: American football (over the top arcade style)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: Arcade sports, with beat-'em-up hit feel and a light story campaign\n- Perspective: Three-quarter camera from the sideline, following the ball, zoomable\n- Tech: my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (commit 4390a9852fe0, with E1, E2, E5), vanilla JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio. Playwright 1.63.0 for browser checks. No CDN or libraries.\n- Art Direction: Engine-native HD Humanoid rigs at res ps1, procedural turf and stands, sprites, particles, lights\n- Animation: Engine Humanoid rig poses (run, down, cheer, wince); no mocap\n- Audio: All music, effects and voices synthesized in code; babble voices for the radio\n- Online: none (not built)\n- Testing: Headless Node VM tests (`test/run.mjs`) and Playwright screenshots (`tools/shots.mjs`)\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium 1243 via Playwright\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** Four: the ball was never marked held, so no tackle or touchdown could end a play and the match stalled; the radio dialog never ticked; a scene change needed a no-fade option for the tests; the Dev mode dialog updated before its scene was entered. Screenshots caught four more: the camera was too close, the controller prompts ran across the field, the hot-streak line used an unsupported glyph, and the radio covered the call hint. Reading the engine caught the missing PlayStation symbols and a roster order mismatch.\n- **How many were critical or game breaking?** One: the stall, which meant no score was possible. It is fixed, and the whole match now runs to the final whistle in every run.\n- **Most helpful test:** The whole-match run, where the CPU calls for both sides through four quarters. It found the stall immediately.\n- **Least helpful test:** The boot suite. It passed first time and checks little.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The Humanoid rig with poses, and the Menu, Dialog and Game APIs. `game.advance` with `game.debug` made the match testable without a browser.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes. Scene changes fade by default, so an unwaited test sees the old scene. The Dialog must be ticked every step, which the API card implies but does not say. The pixel font lacked the PlayStation symbols, and the glyph setting defaulted to Auto. The Menu `y` option is a number, which the card leaves unclear.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** The match simulation: downs, play calls, the QB and throws, catches and picks, carriers, tackles, Big Hits, fumbles, phases, and CPU roles.\n- **Hardest part:** The 67 KB card and the 1.2 MB engine file. Finding the right names for the rig, menus, dialog and settings meant reading the source in several places.\n- **What I changed and why:** E1 adds `✕ ○ □ △` to the pixel font, because controller prompts drew `?`. E2 makes PlayStation the default glyph set, as TASK.md asks. E5 lets a dialog voice be a function, so each letter gets its own pitch for the babble voices.\n- **One thing I'd change:** A dialog that ticks itself from the game loop, so a scene does not have to call it. I'd also like a pad's symbols to work in the font for every label without a patch.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The exit-interview shape and the TASK.md feature list. Together they make a clear checklist.\n- **Confusing:** The plan is over 2,500 lines and names several full systems (online play, a broadcast camera, a story, couch co-op) with no cut order. The folder naming mixes the plan's model name with the STAGE's.\n- **Hardest:** Fitting the whole plan into one session. I built the core match, the cup, the attract mode, the Dev mode, and About, and cut online play, couch co-op, and most of the plan's other systems.\n- **What I'd change:** Add a priority order and a stopping point, such as a must-have list and a list of what may be cut. Say which features the \"done\" condition requires."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1300,"cache_read_input_tokens":265279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1300},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91d88268-7ace-4e56-bce5-4455bcc4424c","uuid":"b9e0cd42-8131-448a-b588-079734eb15c8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:39:26.879Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4RfTK3idVnouaX7D9V"}
